# Title
P0 fix (a): thread pooled HOME into the jail + re-carve slot home after repo ro-bind

# Scope
TWO single-file edits, each a `__JANUSMASK_PATCHES__` SYMBOL patch (do NOT emit
`__JANUSMASK_MANIFEST__`). Each touches one sensitive `harness/**` file → `harness_self_fix`. READ
both files first.

TASK 1 — `harness/agent_jail.py::build_jail_argv` (SYMBOL patch, name `build_jail_argv`):
Today the credential HOME subdirs (`~/.gemini`, `~/.claude`) are rw-bound EARLY (the `_home_subs`
loop, ~lines 183-199) and the repo source ro-bind comes LATER (`argv += ["--ro-bind", repo_root,
repo_root]`, ~line 332). The in-code comment at ~line 168 states the home subdirs are bound first
"so the later repo ro-bind overlays any overlap (the repo lives under HOME)". That overlay is
CORRECT for the operator home (repo is under home), but WRONG for an agy-pool slot home, which
lives UNDER `repo_root` (`<repo>/.agents/agy-pool/wN`) — there the repo ro-bind SHADOWS the slot
home read-only, causing EROFS when the slot's `~/.gemini`/`~/.claude` is written.
FIX: AFTER the repo ro-bind line, add a guarded re-carve mirroring the existing `_gemini_proj`
re-carve pattern ("later bind wins", ~lines 287-289): compute whether the resolved `home` is
STRICTLY under the resolved `repo_root` (e.g. `home_resolved.startswith(repo_root + os.sep)`); ONLY
then, re-emit the rw `--bind` for each credential subdir under that slot home that exists and is
NOT read-only (i.e. `.gemini` and `.claude`, NOT `.nvm` which stays ro) so the later bind wins over
the repo ro-bind. When `home` is the operator home (NOT under repo_root — the pool-disabled / live
default case), the guard is FALSE and NO extra argv is emitted → the argv is BYTE-IDENTICAL to
HEAD. Keep `bind_credentials` semantics: only re-carve credential subdirs when `bind_credentials`
is True (the synthesis path). Preserve the signature and every other byte of the function.

TASK 2 — `harness/orchestrator.py::spawn_agent` (SYMBOL patch, name `spawn_agent`):
At the `agent_jail.build_jail_argv(...)` call (~line 380) add the keyword argument
`home=env.get('HOME')`. The local `env` already carries the pooled slot HOME (set by
`_apply_agy_pool_env` at ~line 275 when the pool is enabled; identical to `os.environ['HOME']` when
the pool is disabled). Add ONLY that one kwarg to that one call. Preserve the signature and every
other byte of `spawn_agent`.

# Inputs
READ `harness/agent_jail.py` and `harness/orchestrator.py`. VERIFIED at HEAD 2cadab5:
- `agent_jail.py:71` `home: str | Path | None = None`; `:107` `home = str(Path(home or os.environ.get("HOME", "/tmp")).resolve())`. The `_home_subs` rw-bind loop is at ~:183-199; the repo ro-bind `argv += ["--ro-bind", repo_root, repo_root]` is at ~:332; the existing "later bind wins" re-carve precedent is `_gemini_proj` at ~:287-289.
- `orchestrator.py:380` calls `agent_jail.build_jail_argv(cmd, repo_root=_jail_repo_root, work_dir=env['JANUSMASK_WORK_DIR'], state_dir=env['JANUSMASK_STATE_DIR'], dbus_proxy_socket=_dbus_sock, extra_ro=_external_jail_extra_ro(_jail_repo_root))` — NO `home=` kwarg today. `_apply_agy_pool_env` (orchestrator.py:212) sets `env['HOME']` to the slot home ONLY when `workers.agy_pool.enabled` (returns env unchanged otherwise).
VERIFIED BYTE-IDENTITY (scripted, `_autowork_scratch/report03_p0_fixa_diag.py`): with the operator home, `build_jail_argv(..., home=os.environ['HOME'])` produces an argv byte-identical to `build_jail_argv(...)` (no home=). With a slot home under repo_root, the current repo ro-bind index (52) comes AFTER the slot `.gemini` rw-bind index (35) — proving the shadow; the fix moves the slot-home rw-bind after the repo ro-bind.

# Non-Goals
Integration is out of scope (the word `integration` MUST appear here to excuse the
integration-test requirement). Do NOT enable `workers.agy_pool.enabled` (it stays false). Do NOT
change any function signature. Do NOT change behavior when `home` is the operator home / the pool
is disabled — the pool-disabled jail argv MUST stay byte-identical to HEAD. Do NOT touch the
`bind_credentials=False` (execute) path's credential-dropping. Do NOT edit any file other than the
one named per task. Do NOT author tests beyond the two oracles.

# Deliverables
`harness/agent_jail.py` with `build_jail_argv` re-carving slot-home credential subdirs after the
repo ro-bind ONLY when `home` is under `repo_root`; `harness/orchestrator.py` with `spawn_agent`
passing `home=env.get('HOME')` into the `build_jail_argv` call. GREEN under the scoped
verification_commands, with the pool-disabled jail argv proven byte-identical to HEAD.

